\description{
Attaches a bootstrap covariance matrix \verb{$Vp} to a fitted \code{\link[=gbgam]{gbgam()}} model.
Each replicate simulates a new response at the fitted means and refits
the model, redoing on its own the steps that \code{mode} names; the covariance
of the replicates' coefficients, widened for smoothing bias unless
\code{alpha = NULL}, becomes \verb{$Vp}. \link[=plot.gbgam]{plot()} and
\link[=predict.gbgam]{predict(se.fit = TRUE)} then use it, with no further
step; \code{\link[=smooth_intervals]{smooth_intervals()}} gives intervals at another level or with
another \code{correction}, and the limits as numbers.
